   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## starter 05 \u00b7 sketch to render\n\n**You need:** Flux 2 Klein 4B as in starter 02.\n\n**Do:** Queue. The sample facade's *sketch_photo* is a phone photo of a pencil sketch: scan to line straightens and\ncleans it, every closed shape becomes a region, coloured dots name them (red = the door, blue = first floor\nwindows), Klein renders the drawing region by region and your line goes back on top.\n\n**Your drawing:** draw on a print of the template (or any paper), photograph it, Load Image into node 2 and link\nwidth / height from *kubakub project settings*. A marker dot in a shape = its name for the rules (`[tag:red]`).\nStrokes don't need to meet: `gap_px` closes gaps. Too many small regions: raise `min_region_area`.\n`denoise` lower = closer to the drawing; line overlay `amount` 0.3 = a light trace, 1 = exactly your stroke.\n"
   ],
   "title": "read me"
  }
